    "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>Photometric CCD observations of the brightest stars in several stellar trapezia (ADS\u00a0719, ADS\u00a01869, ADS\u00a013292, and ADS\u00a013374) are presented. In order to measure the U, B, V, R, and I magnitudes of the stars in trapezia we utilise the aperture photometry technique. This study is performed on images obtained at the Observatorio Astron\u00f3mico Nacional at San Pedro M\u00e1rtir (OAN), Baja California, M\u00e9xico. Comparison of our photometry with published results for IC\u00a01590 (ADS\u00a0719) and Gaia (for all trapezia) is presented. With the $Q=(U-B)-0.72(B-V)$ parameter we obtained the spectral type of the stars as well as their distance to the Sun and their reddening. This work aims to analyse the accuracy of the spectral types derived from the Q parameter for the stars belonging to these trapezia. It is important to emphasise that this is the first step of an extended project to study stellar trapezia, their stellar content, the stars spectral types, and the dynamics of these stars which are subjected to strong dynamical interactions.</jats:p>",
